Rename scalar.c's stub `load_builtin_commands` to avoid colliding with
git.c's real definition when scalar.o is linked into git.exe via the
multicall pipeline.

The function in scalar.c is a dummy `die("not implemented")` stub kept
only so that scalar's standalone executable can satisfy the unresolved
symbol pulled by help.c. Under our multicall build, git.c provides the
real implementation and the stub becomes both unnecessary and an active
hazard (link-time collision) — rename it so the symbol disappears from
scalar.o. Standalone scalar is no longer built in this tree.

--- a/scalar.c
+++ b/scalar.c
@@ -413,11 +413,12 @@ static int delete_enlistment(struct strbuf *enlistment)
 }

 /*
- * Dummy implementation; Using `get_version_info()` would cause a link error
- * without this.
+ * Renamed from `load_builtin_commands` to `scalar_load_builtin_commands`
+ * so this dummy doesn't collide with git.c's real implementation when
+ * scalar.o is folded into git.exe by the unpins multicall pipeline.
  */
-void load_builtin_commands(const char *prefix UNUSED,
-			   struct cmdnames *cmds UNUSED)
+void scalar_load_builtin_commands(const char *prefix UNUSED,
+				  struct cmdnames *cmds UNUSED)
 {
 	die("not implemented");
 }
